Description: Retry openat2 on EAGAIN when chasing paths
 Flatpak 1.16 resolves an extension's merge-dirs with openat2(RESOLVE_BENEATH), which fails
 with EAGAIN when a mount or rename happens anywhere during the lookup. Flatpak then refuses
 to start: "Extension ... has invalid merge-dirs". Upstream libglnx retries (Flatpak 1.18.2
 and later carry it).
Origin: upstream, https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/libglnx/-/commit/eef7f14c344723cb20bebd04dcc79be77363c3be
---
diff --git a/subprojects/libglnx/glnx-chase.c b/subprojects/libglnx/glnx-chase.c
index 2251cb71..49e606a3 100644
--- a/subprojects/libglnx/glnx-chase.c
+++ b/subprojects/libglnx/glnx-chase.c
@@ -684,7 +684,10 @@ glnx_chaseat_full (int                 dirfd,
         .resolve = openat2_resolve,
       };
 
-      fd = openat2 (dirfd, path, &how, sizeof (how));
+      do
+        fd = openat2 (dirfd, path, &how, sizeof (how));
+      while (fd < 0 && errno == EAGAIN);
+
       if (fd < 0)
         {
           /* If the syscall is not implemented (ENOSYS) or blocked by
